{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoPairSaddle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoPairSaddle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_one_sub_ne_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_one_sub_ne_pi","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L383-L391","doc":"`w ∈ notCut` ⟹ `arg (1 − w) ≠ π`: if `Im w ≠ 0` then `Im (1 − w) ≠ 0`, and\notherwise `Re w < 1` puts `1 − w` strictly in the right half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_conj","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L375-L381","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.argSum_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.argSum_conj","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L362-L373","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_div_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_div_conj","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L353-L360","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L341-L351","doc":"On `|x| = 1`, conjugation **swaps** the two mixed arguments. This is the one\nfact the second branch rests on, and it is why mirroring the inequalities\nbranch-by-branch fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.conj_eq_inv_of_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.conj_eq_inv_of_unit","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L328-L339","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_mul_or_div_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_mul_or_div_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L296-L304","doc":"**Regime 3, as one statement.** `Re(x·y) + Re(y/x) = 2cos φ·Re y ≤ 0` gives\nthe disjunction; either side lands inside `(−2π, 2π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_real_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_real_neg","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L271-L294","doc":"**Regime 4 — the real pair.** Past the discriminant crossing both pair roots\nare real and **negative**, so `arg(1−y) = 0` and `arg(−y) = 0` outright and the\nwhole quantity collapses to `arg(1−x·y) + arg(1−y/x)`, inside `(−π, π)` by the two\n`Im` signs.\n\n⚠ This is the regime that needs `sin φ > 0`, through `hmul`/`hdiv`, and it is the\none that breaks at `φ = π`: there `Im(x·y) = 0`, both arguments are `π`, and\n`argSum = 2π` (Route 38 G15). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_div_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_div_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L249-L269","doc":"**Regime 3b — `Re(y/x) ≤ 0`,** the other half of regime 3. Which of the two\nfactors has non-positive real part is not determined by\n`Re(x·y) + Re(y/x) = 2cos φ·Re y ≤ 0`, and does not need to be: the bound is\nsymmetric in them. Interval `(−2π, 2π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_mul_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_mul_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L232-L247","doc":"**Regime 3a — `Re(x·y) ≤ 0`.** Neither `Im`-sign argument applies here; the\nmissing `π/2` comes from `Re(1 − x·y) ≥ 1 > 0` instead. Interval `(−2π, 3π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_im_mul_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_im_mul_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L217-L230","doc":"**Regime 2 — `Re y ≤ 0` and `cos φ ≤ 0`.** Both terms of `Im(x·y)` now flip,\nso `arg(1−x·y) ≥ 0` instead. Interval `(−3π/2, 2π)`; the upper end is reached only\nif `arg(1−y) = 0`, which `Im y > 0` forbids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_lt_of_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L201-L215","doc":"**Regime 1 — `Re y > 0`.** On the arc this forces `cos φ > 0`, and then every\nterm of `Im(x·y) = cos φ·Im y + sin φ·Re y` carries the sign of `Im y`, so\n`arg(1−x·y) < 0`. That is exactly where `im_mul_Ypair_fst_neg` fails (Route 38\nG3): the failure supplies the bound. Interval `(−3π/2, 2π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_Ico_of_re_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_Ico_of_re_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L170-L185","doc":"`Re y ≤ 0` and `Im y > 0` put `arg y` in `[π/2, π)`, hence `−C ∈ (0, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_Ioo_of_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_Ioo_of_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L162-L168","doc":"`Re y > 0` and `Im y > 0` put `arg y` in `(0, π/2)`, hence `−C ∈ (π, 2π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_pi_sub_two_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_pi_sub_two_arg","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L157-L160","doc":"On `Im y > 0`, `arg(−y) = arg y − π`, so `−2·arg(−y) = 2π − 2·arg y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_arg_lt_of_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_arg_lt_of_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L150-L153","doc":"`|arg z| < π/2` whenever `Re z > 0` — the shape regime 3 needs, where the\n`π/2` comes from `Re(x·y) ≤ 0` rather than from a sign of an imaginary part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L146-L148","doc":"`arg z ∈ [0, π]` whenever `Im z ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_pos","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L140-L144","doc":"`arg z ∈ (0, π]` whenever `Im z > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_mem_neg","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L136-L138","doc":"`arg z ∈ (−π, 0)` whenever `Im z < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_one_sub_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_one_sub_mem","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L126-L134","doc":"`arg (1−y) ∈ (−π/2, 0)` whenever `Re y < 1` and `Im y > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_eq_zero_of_argSum_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_eq_zero_of_argSum_bound","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L84-L122","doc":"**The reduction: any bound under `2π` gives `∂V/∂y = 0`.**\n\n`exists_int_dVdy_mul` gives `∂V/∂y·y = −k·2πi`; its imaginary part is\n`−argSum x y = −k·2π`. So `argSum` is an integer multiple of `2π`, and a strict\nbound by `2π` forces the integer to be `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.argSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.argSum","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoPairSaddle.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The quantity `exists_int_dVdy_mul` pins to `2πℤ`: the imaginary part of\n`−∂V/∂y · y`, written out. ","signatureChunk":0}]}